    {
      "id": "RpY5C9WC556OM2g7Mpvfx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3651.2300497663346,
      "y": 3016.8414726409706,
      "width": 654.767333984375,
      "height": 260,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0y",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1861493931,
      "version": 861,
      "versionNonce": 748132235,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1789490786225,
      "created": 1789490057938,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Cache Eviction Policies:\nWhen using cache, one must have eviction policy configured\nvolatile-lru or volatile-ttl: Should have TTL set (matching the rate window length\n+ a buffer) if the cacher runs our of memory redis will only evict keys that have an \nexplicit expiration set\n\nNEVER USE allkeys-lru as it will evict the active keys and reset the counter\n\nStrategy:\n\n(rate:key_123:minute) with TTL matching the window duration\nonce the window expires, redis auto garbage collects\ninactive user consumes 0 bytes of memory outside their active traffic window",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Cache Eviction Policies:\nWhen using cache, one must have eviction policy configured\nvolatile-lru or volatile-ttl: Should have TTL set (matching the rate window length\n+ a buffer) if the cacher runs our of memory redis will only evict keys that have an \nexplicit expiration set\n\nNEVER USE allkeys-lru as it will evict the active keys and reset the counter\n\nStrategy:\n\n(rate:key_123:minute) with TTL matching the window duration\nonce the window expires, redis auto garbage collects\ninactive user consumes 0 bytes of memory outside their active traffic window",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0HyL-LvGQLXlxGWX40auX",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3646.1354064069697,
      "y": 3284.7927499295943,
      "width": 646.0634765625,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 905385579,
      "version": 444,
      "versionNonce": 1861136325,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1789491058960,
      "created": 1789490299827,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "With TTL eviction and Token bucket algo how to execute calculation atomically \nwithout race condition between concurrent requests on same API key\n\nAs redis executes lua scripts single threaded on a given key's shard, the operation\nis non-blocking and completely race-condition-free",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "With TTL eviction and Token bucket algo how to execute calculation atomically \nwithout race condition between concurrent requests on same API key\n\nAs redis executes lua scripts single threaded on a given key's shard, the operation\nis non-blocking and completely race-condition-free",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gD3WzM_fcJZy88spVG528",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3052.8308973377843,
      "y": 3020.408060530574,
      "width": 538.6075439453125,
      "height": 280,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b10",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1412810603,
      "version": 635,
      "versionNonce": 1549848613,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1789494794721,
      "created": 1789490503789,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Choosing Redis over memcached\nRedis-Pros \n- native lua scripting support. Allows executing multi-step \nlogic atomically on the server side in a single network round trip\n- Supports hashes\n- built-in key expiration (TTL)\n\nMemcached-Cons\n- Lack fo server-side logic\n- no complex data structure\n\nThere are others for scale like Valkey, KeyDB, ScyllaDB\n\nWe will use a Sharded Redis Cluster (or Valkey) running in each region",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Choosing Redis over memcached\nRedis-Pros \n- native lua scripting support. Allows executing multi-step \nlogic atomically on the server side in a single network round trip\n- Supports hashes\n- built-in key expiration (TTL)\n\nMemcached-Cons\n- Lack fo server-side logic\n- no complex data structure\n\nThere are others for scale like Valkey, KeyDB, ScyllaDB\n\nWe will use a Sharded Redis Cluster (or Valkey) running in each region",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "osaPGBWFq6-cSEciLOm1h",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3029.3911407152877,
      "y": 4084.881169567726,
      "width": 580.6084922485043,
      "height": 480,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b11",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2123796843,
      "version": 1289,
      "versionNonce": 1325221893,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1789496159193,
      "created": 1789490864136,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Multi Region Synchronization Strategy:\n\nif a user makes requests in us-east and eu-west at the exact same\nsecond:\n\nOption A\nAll regional API gateways execute lua scripts against a single global redis\ncluser\n-> Single global cluster means increased latency and can go beyond\nrequired metrics\n-> Also Single Point of Failure\n\nOption B\nEach region run its own redis cluster and asynchronously sync counter\nupdates to other regions\n-> inconsistency in redis in case multiple requests go to different regions\n-> will go beyond the acceptable limit\n\nOption C\nToken reservation/partitoning: Allocate a quota split to each region\ndynamically (like 50% us-east and 50% eu-west)\n-> Dynamic Quota Partitioning avoids cross-region network round trips on\nthe critical request path\nby turning a global rate-limiting problem into localized sub-problems.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Multi Region Synchronization Strategy:\n\nif a user makes requests in us-east and eu-west at the exact same second:\n\nOption A\nAll regional API gateways execute lua scripts against a single global redis cluser\n-> Single global cluster means increased latency and can go beyond required metrics\n-> Also Single Point of Failure\n\nOption B\nEach region run its own redis cluster and asynchronously sync counter updates to other regions\n-> inconsistency in redis in case multiple requests go to different regions\n-> will go beyond the acceptable limit\n\nOption C\nToken reservation/partitoning: Allocate a quota split to each region dynamically (like 50% us-east and 50% eu-west)\n-> Dynamic Quota Partitioning avoids cross-region network round trips on the critical request path\nby turning a global rate-limiting problem into localized sub-problems.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "38tetVVwXgM5DZdC_jgQC",
      "type": "text",
